Assumption: host injects normalize via setNormalize; if host instead passes normalize directly to tokenize, adapt in round 2 based on peer broadcasts.
Plan round 2: coordinate with pipeline.js author on interface (tokenize output array of strings, empty array for empty/whitespace-only input).",
"message": "tokenizer.js round 1 done. tokenize(text) applies the injected normalize(text) (host should call setNormalize(fn) to wire it), then extracts tokens with /[A-Za-z0-9]+(?:'[A-Za-z0-9]+)*/g. Contract for pipeline.js: tokenize returns an array of strings in input order; empty array for empty/whitespace-only input; no stopwords; negations preserved; apostrophe runs kept as single tokens (e.g. don't, can't). Frequencies in pipeline should use plain Object.create(null) or hasOwnProperty to stay safe with keys like 'constructor'. Happy to adjust the injection mechanism if the host wires normalize differently."
